abstract: >-
  Sovereign Agent Fleet is a local-first cognitive control plane that governs
  probabilistic agents and their consequential actions. It separates cognition
  (what a model believes) from authority (what the system is permitted to do)
  from execution (what actually happened), and keeps them in separate
  computational boundaries so a model output is never mistaken for a permission.
  The frozen deterministic authorization function fleet.epistemic.decide()
  decides every consequential action; the model only proposes. Five
  architectural invariants and a six-adversary threat model (A1-A6) are backed
  by a 567-test passing suite, a 6,000-point parametric sweep, and a genuinely
  blind 5,000-vector adversary harness.
